                <div class="mt-16">
                  <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
                    Common Mistakes When Buying Rockwell Tools
                  </h2>

                  <p>
                    Rockwell sits between store brands and the major professional lines, and the buying mistakes come from misjudging which side of that line a given tool falls on.
                  </p>

                  <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the Specialty Tools for General Work</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        Rockwell's distinctive tools — compact multi-tools and unusual saw formats — are genuinely clever within their niche and compromised outside it. Bought as a general-purpose replacement for a conventional tool, they frequently disappoint. Buy them for the specific job they solve.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting Professional-Duty Longevity</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        The line is engineered and priced for homeowners and light trade use. Under daily job-site loads the motors and mechanisms wear faster than professional-tier equivalents. That is a fair trade at the price, provided you are not expecting otherwise.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Overlooking Battery Platform Lock-In</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        Adding a Rockwell cordless tool means another battery chemistry, another charger, and another set of packs to keep charged. Where you already own a mature platform, the total cost of adding one Rockwell tool is higher than the sticker suggests.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not Checking Accessory Availability</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        Some Rockwell tools use proprietary blades, bases, or accessories that are harder to source than standard fittings. Check what the consumables cost and where you can buy them before committing — that is where an inexpensive tool can become an expensive one.
                      </p>
                    </div>
